    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="1092" n="986" xml:id="pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-24T17:00:00+03:00">October 24, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 24—12:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>793. My 789, October 24, 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">9</hi>] a.m. I saw Potemkin
                    at 3 o’clock this afternoon. He stated that he had no other information than
                    appeared in the Tass despatch quoted in my telegram under reference but that in
                    anticipation of my call he had requested the Soviet naval authorities at
                    Murmansk to let him have a full report as quickly as possible and that he would
                    advise me as soon as all of the facts were in his possession.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
